EXPERIMENT 1 – IDENTIFICATION AND DOCUMENTATION OF SOFTWARE DEFECTS IN ATM SYSTEM

AIM
To examine an ATM system specification, identify software defects and document them using black-box testing techniques.

ALGORITHM
1. Select the ATM system and study its specifications.
2. Identify features such as card validation, PIN verification and cash withdrawal.
3. Prepare test cases with valid and invalid inputs.
4. Execute each test case and compare expected and actual results.
5. Identify and confirm defects by repeating failed test cases.
6. Record defect ID, description, severity, priority and screenshots.

CODE
This is a manual testing experiment. No programming code is required.

INPUT
Parameter	Input
Card	Valid ATM card
PIN	1234
Account balance	₹25,000
Transaction limit	₹10,000
Daily limit	₹40,000
Withdrawal amount	₹5,000

OUTPUT
Test Case	Expected Result	Status
Valid card and PIN	Login successful	Pass
Invalid PIN	Error message displayed	Pass
Withdrawal ₹5,000	Cash withdrawal successful	Pass
Withdrawal ₹10,100	Transaction rejected	Pass
Withdrawal ₹250	Invalid denomination rejected	Pass

RESULT
Thus, the ATM system was tested using manual black-box testing. Test cases were executed, and software defects were identified and documented successfully.
